From ab879723ee55da2b4a195119244da01986e07696 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:52:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 35/87] h713: contract v5: the contract page in one table in
 platform/memory.h

The layout of the contract page was spread over memory.h, hdmi.c
(EINT_SEEN), css.c (RVBAR_SEEN) and r-ccu.c (LOSC_SEEN), and nothing
said who writes a word, who zeroes it and what survives a restart
(PRUEFUNG5 F15). platform/memory.h now carries the whole page as
version 5 lays it out: the classes R, D, S, K, A, P and X with writer,
zeroing and lifetime, the K block (crust's record across its restarts:
compat, build2, standby state, net words, error bits, counters, cycle,
wake time), the A block the ARM writes (net request, budget, confirm,
TF-A word), the phases, causes, error bits and counter bytes. The
three drivers use its names for the S words; nothing moves.

Two comments are corrected: crust's block lies inside the vendor
blob's code, data and stack, so a switch is always a reset and a full
reload (N-09), and the MIPS writes user1 sub-block 1, which the HDMI
module reads directly (F15).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
